ca02eb88-dde8-4760-85d5-30281c375485	pathology_micro	BDS-I	A gram-positive bacillus is identified as an obligate anaerobe that produces "sulfur granules" in clinical samples. Which culture medium is best suited for its identification?	{"LJ Media","Sabouraud Dextrose Agar","Robertson Cooked Meat Media","TCBS Agar"}	2	Actinomycetes (e.g., A. israelii) are strict anaerobes and produce sulfur granules. RCM is the standard medium for isolating anaerobic bacteria .	Bacteriology	\N
