7fa21052-7c6c-4722-90dd-6060db448440	pathology_micro	BDS-I	Bacillus cereus food poisoning can present in two forms. The emetic strain is most commonly associated with the consumption of:	{"Canned meat",Honey,"Chinese fried rice","Dairy products"}	2	The emetic strain of B. cereus (incubation 1-6 hrs) is typically caused by contaminated Chinese fried rice .	Food Poisoning	\N
31415bdc-0e76-43d5-ba7d-3eff90acac4f	pathology_micro	BDS-I	"Stormy fermentation" in litmus milk is a characteristic laboratory finding for which organism?	{"Clostridium tetani","Clostridium perfringens","Bacillus anthracis","Staph aureus"}	1	Clostridium perfringens causes immense fermentation of litmus milk, known as stormy fermentation .	Bacteriology	\N
07b0656c-812a-4035-8deb-430914cec555	pathology_micro	BDS-I	Tetanospasmin causes spastic paralysis by acting pre-synaptically. Which inhibitory neurotransmitters does it primarily inhibit?	{Acetylcholine,"GABA and Glycine",Dopamine,Serotonin}	1	Tetanospasmin prevents the release of inhibitory neurotransmitters GABA and Glycine, leading to constant muscle stimulation (LockJaw) .	Bacterial Toxins	\N
