9f565979-19d2-4980-b657-bf7b63dbb89c	pathology_micro	BDS-I	Clostridium difficile associated diarrhea (CDAD) is most commonly a side effect of long-term use of which antibiotic group?	{Penicillins,"3rd generation cephalosporins/Clindamycin",Aminoglycosides,Tetracyclines}	1	CDAD is associated with long-term use of 3rd generation cephalosporins and Clindamycin, which destroy normal flora .	Clinical Bacteriology	\N
