9667fd2c-f096-4dd2-9f3a-8c017d8374ef	materials	BDS-I	Yttria-stabilized tetragonal zirconia polycrystal (Y-TZP) is susceptible to "low-temperature degradation." This phenomenon is characterized by:	{"Rapid tetragonal-to-monoclinic transformation in dry heat","Slow superficial t→m transformation in a humid atmosphere","Monoclinic-to-cubic transformation at 70°C","Loss of strength due to stress corrosion by nitrogen molecules"}	1	Low-temperature degradation (aging) occurs in Y-TZP near 250°C and even in water/steam at lower temperatures (70°C-130°C). It involves a slow superficial t→m transformation leading to micro-cracking and loss of strength.	Dental Ceramics	\N
