b5223d36-6c6b-489b-a329-8ccbb867eb35	materials	BDS-I	Which "Smart" material property of GIC is most beneficial in an acidic (cariogenic) environment?	{"Increased translucency","Chemical bond to enamel","Release of fluoride ions when pH drops","High compressive strength"}	2	GICs are smart materials because they can release more fluoride ions when the surrounding pH drops, providing anti-cariogenic effects when most needed.	Glass Ionomer Cements	\N
59e0a44e-5369-4039-976a-984ce22685a8	materials	BDS-I	In "Wet-Field" bonding, if the dentin is over-dried, why does the patient experience pain upon restoration placement?	{"Acid penetration is deeper","Resin monomers become toxic","The cement withdraws water from the dentinal tubules","The hybrid layer becomes too thick"}	2	Over-drying dentin causes the cement (especially GIC) to withdraw water from the dentinal tubules to satisfy its setting reaction, leading to pain.	Glass Ionomer Cements	\N
49ab4bfc-a390-4b04-908b-f7904efaf576	materials	BDS-I	"Zirconia" (Y-TZP) is called "Law-tolerant" (or "Flaw-tolerant") because of:	{"Its white color","Its high solubility","Transformation Toughening","Its low elastic modulus"}	2	Transformation toughening occurs when the tetragonal phase transforms to the monoclinic phase near a crack, increasing volume and "pinching" the crack shut.	Dental Ceramics	\N
