a32010fb-4c56-4726-b74f-0b4fc204f1e0	materials	BDS-I	Why is Bis-GMA preferred over Methyl Methacrylate (MMA) in composite resin matrices despite its high viscosity?	{"It is more translucent","It has a larger monomeric molecule resulting in less shrinkage","It contains more fluoride","It does not require a coupling agent"}	1	Bis-GMA molecules are substantially larger than MMA molecules. This results in significantly less polymerization shrinkage during the setting reaction.	Composite Resins	\N
925477b6-a6b2-44e5-a2ab-c597e6fb3232	materials	BDS-I	Which optical property describes the preferential scattering of blue light by nanoparticles in a composite, giving it a life-like appearance?	{Metamerism,Fluorescence,Opalescence,Chroma}	2	Nanoparticles in some composites preferentially scatter blue light when placed against a dark background. This creates an opalescent effect similar to natural tooth enamel.	Optical Properties	\N
cb3046fc-8fdc-424c-8ca2-6d4c16b40754	materials	BDS-I	Why are Silicate cements contraindicated for use in patients who are "mouth breathers"?	{"High fluoride release","Extreme transparency","Dehydration increases brittleness","High risk of secondary caries"}	2	Silicate cement matrices contain a specific amount of liquid. Evaporation of this liquid due to mouth breathing drastically increases the material's brittleness and reduces its optical properties.	Silicate Cements	\N
f84f0e05-46b9-43d8-a5c7-10a74d4b87be	materials	BDS-I	In "High Copper Amalgams," which type of fracture is most common according to clinical observations?	{"Marginal fracture","Bulk fracture","Edge fracture","Creep fracture"}	1	Unlike low-copper amalgams, high-copper amalgam fracture is typically a bulk fracture rather than a marginal breakdown.	Dental Amalgam	\N
50a83170-e776-4b65-9c52-a9084ee280f4	materials	BDS-I	What is the "Achilles heel" of layered Zirconia crowns compared to traditional Metal-Ceramic (PFM) restorations?	{"Core fracture","Poor marginal fit","Chip fracture of the veneering porcelain","Chemical solubility"}	2	While zirconia core fractures are rare, the veneering ceramic is prone to cohesive chip fractures. Layered zirconia crowns fracture at a rate estimated to be five times higher than PFM crowns.	Dental Ceramics	\N
8f108a38-bc8c-4f75-880e-ac73c80c0ea4	materials	BDS-I	In dental materials, "Thixotropy" is an application of which phenomenon?	{"Increase in viscosity under pressure","Decrease in viscosity when external pressure is applied","Expansion upon heating","Chemical bonding to enamel"}	1	Thixotropic materials, like some impression materials and cements, become fluid when external force/pressure is applied and increase in viscosity once the force is removed.	Rheology	\N
