5aba4010-4a19-4b91-b470-a2f20512a99a	materials	BDS-I	In "Addition Silicone" impression materials, what is the clinical risk of pouring the cast immediately?	{"Material expansion","Voids caused by hydrogen gas release","Setting inhibition","High solubility"}	1	A secondary reaction between moisture and residual hydrides can lead to hydrogen gas formation. Pouring the cast too soon results in voids; clinicians should wait at least one hour.	Impression Materials	\N
90bea858-762d-4545-85c8-4a5e1296122e	materials	BDS-I	Which specific generation of bonding agents first combined the primer and adhesive into a single bottle (2-step etch-and-rinse)?	{"3rd Generation","4th Generation","5th Generation","7th Generation"}	2	The 5th generation of dentin bonding agents combined the primer and adhesive into one bottle, following a separate etching step.	Adhesion History	\N
eddf9e04-1b9a-4e04-8c5e-9b3d191e7ca6	materials	BDS-I	What is the primary cause of "Postoperative Sensitivity" in Class I composite restorations according to the "Hydrostatic" theory?	{"Acid etching","Thermal conductivity","Polymerization shrinkage creating a fluid-filled gap","Leaching of HEMA"}	2	Composite resin shrinks and pulls away from the cavity floor, creating a void that fills with fluid. This void causes hydrostatic pressure in the tubules, leading to sensitivity.	Composite Resins	\N
7410d579-4954-4135-afd3-e200eb5ed82c	materials	BDS-I	Which "Smart Material" prevents demineralization by converting to Hydroxyapatite when the salivary pH drops below critical levels?	{GIC,"Shape Memory Alloys","Smart Composites with ACP",Zirconia}	2	Smart composites containing Amorphous Calcium Phosphate (ACP) convert to hydroxyapatite and precipitate within seconds when the pH drops, preventing local demineralization.	Smart Materials	\N
efc5c9f4-05c0-4c24-8926-48112fd147e4	materials	BDS-I	In "Direct Filling Gold" restorations, what is the clinical purpose of heating the gold (degassing) until it is dull red?	{"To make it melt","To drive off adsorbed gases like ammonia","To increase its weight","To change its color to match the tooth"}	1	Degassing (or "annealing") involves heating the gold to drive off adsorbed gases (e.g., ammonia) that would otherwise prevent the gold from being cohesive.	Direct Filling Gold	\N
1db95731-42f5-49f1-a698-26c6e5e28c0f	materials	BDS-I	Why are GICs contraindicated for luting "All-Ceramic" crowns despite their chemical bond?	{"Low fluoride release","High solubility","Water sorption creates \\"Hoop stress\\"","High modulus of elasticity"}	2	GICs (and RMGICs) absorb water and expand. This expansion induces tensile stresses (Hoop stress) that can fracture brittle all-ceramic crowns.	Dental Ceramics	\N
451bf86a-824f-4a97-a6fa-d1c8906d6f3a	materials	BDS-I	When using "Self-Etch" adhesives, what is a known long-term risk related to their hydrophilic nature?	{"Excessive enamel etching","Formation of \\"water trees\\" and hydrolytic degradation","High postoperative sensitivity","Chemical toxicity to the pulp"}	1	The acidic and hydrophilic nature of self-etch adhesives attracts water, forming "water trees". These water-filled channels lead to leaching and hydrolytic degradation of the hybrid layer.	Adhesion & Degradation	\N
a4f58849-9466-4a4c-b529-bdc42c7c6aca	materials	BDS-I	In "Amalgam Restorations," the cavosurface angle should ideally be:	{"45 degrees","90 degrees","120 degrees","30 degrees"}	1	Because amalgam is brittle and has low edge strength, a 90-degree (butt-joint) marginal configuration is mandatory to prevent fracture.	Cavity Preparation	\N
cc07bbb0-1288-437a-a0e5-bd133c9e2c8e	materials	BDS-I	Which component is added to "Dental Porcelain" specifically to match its CTE with that of a metal coping?	{Kaolin,Quartz,Leucite,"Boric acid"}	2	Leucite is added to glass ceramics to increase their coefficient of thermal expansion, ensuring they expand and contract at rates similar to the metal substrate.	Dental Ceramics	\N
