03ad4e94-bf95-4d27-a63e-fe8e5c918694	materials	BDS-I	Which form of Caries removal involves leaving "Firm Dentin" to be remineralized?	{"Complete excavation","Stepwise Excavation / SCR","Total Etch","Fissure sealants"}	1	(SCR - Selective Caries Removal) Firm dentin has lost mineral but retains its collagen structure; if isolated, it can remineralize and should be left in place.	Caries Management	\N
83bc7f09-2178-49f2-9ece-06e1e1d0346b	materials	BDS-I	In "Investment Materials," what is "Inversion"?	{"The material shrinking upon cooling","A change in crystalline form (alpha to beta) at a specific temperature","The loss of water from the binder","A reaction with the casting alloy"}	1	Inversion expansion occurs when the refractory material changes from an alpha to a beta crystalline form at a specific temperature, providing sudden expansion.	Investment Materials	\N
21b8a5b1-35b3-4976-a4e3-1c400d078e13	materials	BDS-I	"Lava Ultimate" is a nanoceramic material. According to the sources, it is contraindicated for which application?	{Inlays,Onlays,Crowns,Veneers}	2	Lava Ultimate is indicated for inlays and onlays but is specifically noted as NOT for crowns.	CAD/CAM Materials	\N
e7c652dc-a723-4002-894b-47ee09a33b96	materials	BDS-I	Why does "Strontium-based" GIC provide better radiopacity than "Calcium-based" GIC?	{"It contains more silica","Strontium has a higher atomic number (38 vs 20)","It has a faster setting time","It is more translucent"}	1	Heavy metals with high atomic numbers, such as Strontium (38), have more electrons to absorb X-rays compared to Calcium (20).	GIC Properties	\N
3b024d06-f97b-4645-b3ae-6daec752c5b9	materials	BDS-I	In the "Total-Etch" (Etch-and-Rinse) technique, what is the consequence of over-drying the dentin after acid application?	{"Increased bond strength","Collapse of the collagen network","Improved primer penetration","Reduced postoperative sensitivity"}	1	(Noted as a concept in materials turn 1) Over-drying after etching causes the demineralized collagen network to collapse, preventing the primer and bonding agent from infiltrating and forming a hybrid layer.	Dentin Bonding	\N
43246131-14f0-4213-8944-3e4de11bbf42	materials	BDS-I	Which property describes the rate at which thermal changes are conducted through a material, potentially leading to pulpal shock?	{"Thermal Diffusivity","Specific Heat","Thermal Conductivity",CTE}	2	Thermal conductivity is the rate at which heat passes through a material; materials like gold or amalgam are excellent conductors compared to tooth structure.	Physical Properties	\N
b29ab117-7afe-4d94-9766-c141b9bbc092	materials	BDS-I	"C-Factor" logic: Which restoration has the most "free" or unrestrained surface to relieve polymerization stress?	{"Class I","Class II","Class IV","Facial Veneer"}	3	A direct facial veneer is bonded to only one surface, allowing stresses to be relieved by flow from all other unrestrained surfaces.	Adhesion & C-Factor	\N
d3eaf120-b5a1-4034-be4c-fc83553d871e	materials	BDS-I	"Fully Stabilized" monolithic zirconia (Bruxzir Anterior) has improved translucency but suffers from what major disadvantage?	{"Increased solubility","50% reduction in flexural strength","Rapid wear of opposing teeth","High moisture sensitivity"}	1	While fully stabilized zirconia is more translucent, it is accompanied by a significant 50% reduction in its flexural strength.	Dental Ceramics	\N
