e8359cf8-0e9d-4234-a91a-8bfb22a056d1	materials	BDS-I	When preparing a Class I cavity for dental amalgam, the "Axis of Preparation" should be:	{"Parallel to the long axis of the tooth","Parallel to the DEJ","Aligned with the long axis of the crown","Perpendicular to the occlusal plane"}	2	In mandibular posterior teeth, the crown is tilted lingually. Therefore, the axis of the preparation must align with the long axis of the crown, not the whole tooth, to avoid pulpal exposure.	Fundamentals of Tooth Preparation	\N
63f21771-cf9a-47bf-a702-13bbbb1f7fa4	materials	BDS-I	"Firm dentin" differs from "soft dentin" in Selective Caries Removal (SCR) because it:	{"Is heavily infected with bacteria","Has lost its structural collagen","Can be remineralized if sealed","Is always found at the DEJ"}	2	Firm dentin is demineralized but the collagen remains intact. If isolated from the environment, it can remineralize and should be left to avoid pulpal exposure.	Caries Management	\N
7cc2d730-d2d4-4d15-8c0b-c71e5a4b1b95	materials	BDS-I	In the context of "Metamerism," which of the following is true for shade selection?	{"A tooth looks different due to its opalescence","Two objects match under one light source but differ under another","Blue light is scattered by nanoparticles","The intensity of the color increases"}	1	Metamerism is an optical phenomenon where spectral reflectance differs between objects, but they appear identical under specific light sources.	Color and Shade Matching	\N
