dc19bb8c-77d3-47d8-b989-017944f9e69c	prosthodontics	BDS-I	For successful metal-ceramic bonding, Shillingburg states the optimum difference between the coefficients of thermal expansion of the metal and porcelain should be no greater than:	{"$0.5 \\\\times 10^{-6}/^{\\\\circ}C$","$1 \\\\times 10^{-6}/^{\\\\circ}C$","$1.7 \\\\times 10^{-6}/^{\\\\circ}C$","$2.4 \\\\times 10^{-6}/^{\\\\circ}C$"}	1	While a difference of $1.7 \\times 10^{-6}/^{\\circ}C$ can cause failure, the optimum difference to ensure the porcelain "draws" toward the metal is $1 \\times 10^{-6}/^{\\circ}C$.	Metal-Ceramic Bonding	\N
0e3e04a5-42e8-408c-aa47-6fc8d796d608	prosthodontics	BDS-I	According to Stewart, if a mandibular major connector has less than 8 mm of space between the floor of the mouth and the gingival margins, which design is indicated?	{"Lingual Bar","Labial Bar","Lingual Plate","Double Lingual Bar"}	2	A lingual plate is indicated when there is insufficient room (<8 mm) for a lingual bar or when there are high frenum attachments.	RPD Major Connectors	\N
0d1ae956-3943-4cd0-b3a4-a8a9f1c2d754	prosthodontics	BDS-I	When planning an abutment for a fixed partial denture, what is the minimum acceptable crown-root ratio under normal circumstances?	{2:3,1:1,1:2,3:1}	1	The optimum ratio is 2:3, but 1:1 is the minimum ratio acceptable under normal circumstances.	C:R Ratio	\N
f99ff49a-0d09-4869-bf6c-3c3ad7274151	prosthodontics	BDS-I	In a Class III soft palate configuration (Winkler), the soft palate turns downward sharply at what angle to the hard palate?	{"10 degrees","45 degrees","70 degrees","90 degrees"}	2	Class I is horizontal, Class II is at 45°, and Class III is at 70°, making it the least favorable for a posterior palatal seal.	Palatal Seal	\N
da2b2f55-892c-45c0-8992-67afd5979a87	prosthodontics	BDS-I	The "push stroke" with a No. 9 Molt elevator is identified as the most efficient for reflecting a flap. Which source (from previous sessions) and concept from Shillingburg mirrors this focus on clean reflection?	{Electrosurgery,"Rotary Curettage","Gingival Grafting","Chemical Retraction"}	1	Shillingburg notes that rotary curettage removes epithelium with little detectable trauma, but like the "push stroke," it requires inflammation-free tissue.	Soft Tissue Mgmt	\N
4b3af3ff-8156-4c34-bdcb-64b97f2bc589	prosthodontics	BDS-I	Biomechanically, flexibility of an RPD clasp arm is directly proportional to:	{"The width of the arm","The thickness of the arm","The cube of its length","The square of its thickness"}	2	Based on the formula for a cantilever beam, deflection (flexibility) is directly proportional to the cube of the length ($L^3$).	Clasp Design	\N
0a428ebf-9689-4869-bba0-d8851e98a52b	prosthodontics	BDS-I	For Type III gold alloys, the ADA specification requires a minimum elongation of:	{0.05,0.1,0.12,0.25}	2	Type III alloys must have a yield strength between 200–340 MPa and an elongation of at least 12%.	Dental Alloys	\N
011efccc-0606-4a05-83e5-66c27ab6923e	prosthodontics	BDS-I	When using Ferric Sulfate (Astringedent) for tissue management, for how many minutes should the impregnated cord remain in the sulcus?	{"1 minute","3 minutes","5 minutes","10 minutes"}	1	According to the source, the plain knitted cord soaked in ferric sulfate should be removed after 3 minutes.	Hemostasis	\N
a2acdf29-d840-4f69-8235-5854e2c0d106	prosthodontics	BDS-I	In the McLean physiologic impression technique, the ridge portion is recorded in its functional form by:	{"Using a mucostatic wax","Placing an occlusal load on the tray","Using a low-viscosity plaster","Recording the tissues at rest"}	1	This technique records the ridge in functional form by placing an occlusal load on the tray during the procedure.	CD Impressions	\N
fc28d1c4-791e-4724-959c-a8c801261c9c	prosthodontics	BDS-I	What is the optimum film thickness for Zinc Phosphate cement to allow for proper seating and escape?	{"10–20 µm","30–40 µm","50–70 µm","100 µm"}	1	The optimum film thickness for zinc phosphate is approximately 30 to 40 µm.	Luting Agents	\N
1d78fa79-56e0-4d8d-939e-2e2cf7596ac9	prosthodontics	BDS-I	Biomechanically, if the thickness of a fixed partial denture pontic is reduced by one-half, how is the deflection affected?	{"2 times as much","4 times as much","8 times as much","27 times as much"}	2	Deflection is inversely proportional to the cube of the thickness ($1/T^3$). Reducing thickness by half ($0.5^3$) results in 8 times as much deflection.	FPD Biomechanics	\N
b52773a5-a749-4d42-a966-b05e2393ba36	prosthodontics	BDS-I	In the Two-Phase Theory of osteogenesis, Phase II bone regeneration typically begins during the:	{"First 24 hours","Second week","First month","After functional loading"}	1	Phase II involves host-derived angiogenesis and fibroblastic proliferation starting in the second week.	Bone Grafting	\N
699f2073-f916-4632-a239-492358301cfa	prosthodontics	BDS-I	In Applegate’s rules for Kennedy Classification, why is Rule 4 clinically significant for treatment planning?	{"It mandates replacing third molars","It allows ignoring missing second molars not to be replaced","It defines modification spaces","It requires classification after extractions"}	1	Rule 4 states that if a second molar is missing and not to be replaced, it is not considered in the classification, preventing unnecessary modification space designations.	Classification	\N
119a8e7e-5f04-4a72-97cb-22beba4c1d29	prosthodontics	BDS-I	According to Winkler, what is the specific neuron-to-muscle-fiber ratio for the muscles of mastication, indicating their precision level?	{1:3,"1:700 to 1:900",0.7361111111111112,1.4305555555555556}	1	Extrinsic eye muscles are 1:3 (highly precise); leg muscles are 1:1000. Masticatory muscles are intermediate at 1:700-900 muscle fibers per motor unit.	Physiology	\N
95391972-28aa-492d-be8e-111a40fd2687	prosthodontics	BDS-I	When preparing an endodontically treated tooth for a dowel, what is the minimum length of apical fill that must remain to maintain a seal?	{"1 mm","2 mm","4 mm","6 mm"}	2	While the dowel should be 2/3 the root length, the remaining apical fill (AF) must be at least 4.0 mm to ensure the endodontic seal is not compromised.	Post and Core	\N
24461c59-a56c-4948-aa5d-18e3f85b4e87	prosthodontics	BDS-I	In the chemistry of gypsum, how much water is chemically required for 100 g of dental stone to react and form calcium sulfate dihydrate?	{"15.0 mL","18.61 mL","27.0 mL","30.0 mL"}	1	All gypsum products require exactly 18.61 mL of water per 100 g of powder for the chemical reaction; any additional water reduces compressive strength.	Dental Materials	\N
54cf658c-0267-4b90-8237-89755306009a	prosthodontics	BDS-I	Using Shillingburg’s "Golden Proportion" in esthetics, if the width of the maxillary lateral incisor is 1.0, what is the proportional width of the central incisor?	{0.618,1,1.618,2.618}	2	In the golden proportion, the central incisor should be 1.618 times the width of the lateral incisor when viewed from the facial.	Dental Esthetics	\N
