d4e5f97c-9501-44ac-bf31-25a861456119	prosthodontics	BDS-I	A modified 15-8-8 binangle chisel (RS-1) is recommended for radial shoulders. How does it differ from a conventional 15-8-8 chisel?	{"It uses a push stroke","It has hoe blades at both ends","It has a chisel blade at both ends","It is used for subgingival prep"}	1	Unlike the conventional chisel (one hoe/pull, one chisel/push), the RS-1 has a hoe (pull stroke) blade at both ends to avoid nicks and ensure a smooth radial shoulder.	Instrumentation	\N
ec031713-c1ac-4823-8692-c09616b77af6	prosthodontics	BDS-I	For a patient with a Class III interarch relationship, how should the mandibular posterior teeth be arranged relative to the maxillary teeth?	{"Normal buccal-lingual relation","In a \\"crossbite\\" relationship","With 33-degree cusps","Edge-to-edge only"}	1	In Class III (prognathic) situations, the mandibular teeth are often buccal to the maxillary teeth, necessitating a crossbite arrangement for stability.	Occlusion	\N
