d69977c9-8cd5-4f30-882d-8c1f2cca67b0	prosthodontics	BDS-I	Biomechanically, if a clinician decreases the thickness of an RPD clasp arm by half, its flexibility:	{Doubles,Quadruples,"Increases 8 times","Decreases 8 times"}	2	Flexibility (deflection) is inversely proportional to the cube of the thickness. Halving thickness increases flexibility 8 times [173, Turn 11 Logic].	RPD Mechanics	\N
76112f12-c669-492c-bfd1-08687cbd989b	prosthodontics	BDS-I	When using Type III dental stone, what is the resulting compressive strength if the water-powder ratio is 30 mL per 100 g instead of the recommended 27 mL?	{"4,500 psi","4,000 psi","3,000 psi","1,500 psi"}	2	Seemingly small increases in water reduce strength; using 30 mL instead of 27 mL drops the strength from 4,500 psi to 3,000 psi.	Dental Materials	\N
7bbb6867-0285-4a24-8003-8efb9df3949f	prosthodontics	BDS-I	In the arrangement of anterior teeth, "clicking" of the dentures in the elderly is often a result of:	{"Decreased vertical dimension","Muscular incoordination or habit","Use of resin teeth","Poor posterior palatal seal"}	1	Even with correct vertical dimension, "clicking" may occur due to muscular incoordination or habit; using resin teeth can minimize the noise.	CD Troubleshooting	\N
