7d0a17a6-3d3d-4ac1-ab00-3ab19280eca2	prosthodontics	BDS-I	Biomechanically, if the thickness of a gold alloy FPD pontic is reduced by half, how is the deflection of the span affected under a constant load?	{"2 times as much","4 times as much","8 times as much","27 times as much"}	2	Deflection is inversely proportional to the cube of the thickness ($1/T^3$). Therefore, reducing thickness by half ($1/0.5^3$) results in 8 times the deflection.	FPD Biomechanics	\N
0b810433-96b3-400c-9b5b-b996e3aff924	prosthodontics	BDS-I	In terms of neuromuscular precision, how does the ratio of motor neurons to muscle fibers in the muscles of mastication compare to other muscle groups?	{"Equal to extrinsic eye muscles (1:3)","Greater than leg muscles (>1:1000)","Intermediate (1:700–900)","Identical to leg muscles (1:1000)"}	2	Precision is based on innervation ratios. Masticatory muscles are intermediate (1:700–900), less precise than eye muscles (1:3) but more precise than leg muscles (1:1000).	Physiology	\N
