68770f04-6d31-4bfc-9378-83464838a14e	prosthodontics	BDS-I	Shillingburg identifies "Ante's Law" as a guideline for abutment selection. What is the primary reason long-span FPDs fail according to modern biomechanical views?	{"Simple root surface area overload","Leverage and torque","Lack of patient hygiene","Pulpal necrosis"}	1	While root area is important, long-span failures are more often attributed to leverage and torque than to simple overload of the PDL.	FPD Design	\N
