65ead77b-7fe9-4707-8ede-999099ea4fda	orthodontics	BDS-I	The "leeway space" averages approximately how many millimeters per side in the maxillary arch?	{"0.5 mm","1.5 mm","2.5 mm","3.5 mm"}	1	Because primary molars are larger than the premolars that replace them, the leeway space averages about 1.5 mm per side in the maxilla.	Space Relationships	\N
f7390222-e4b1-4685-af4e-474ff47583ae	orthodontics	BDS-I	The "leeway space" averages approximately how many millimeters per side in the mandibular arch?	{"0.5 mm","1.5 mm","2.5 mm","4.5 mm"}	2	Because primary mandibular second molars are significantly larger than second premolars, the leeway space averages about 2.5 mm per side in the mandible.	Space Relationships	\N
