87cf1a63-45d9-4f6c-a73b-77bdb0c6337c	orthodontics	BDS-I	The "incisor liability" refers to the fact that permanent incisors are larger than primary incisors. Which mechanism is NOT utilized to gain space for them?	{"Slight increase in arch width across the canines.","Labial positioning of the permanent incisors.","Repositioning of mandibular canines backward into primate spaces.","Elongation of the anterior mandibular symphysis via bone apposition."}	3	The mechanisms to overcome incisor liability include arch width increase, labial positioning, and use of primate spaces. The anterior symphysis does not undergo apposition to lengthen the arch.	Mixed Dentition	\N
3a9dbd09-19aa-46b4-9a51-4d9792a11180	orthodontics	BDS-I	During the transition from the mixed to the permanent dentition, the total arch length (midline to first molars) typically:	{Increases,"Remains exactly the same",Decreases,Doubles}	2	Arch length decreases primarily due to the mesial drift of the permanent first molars into the leeway space as primary molars exfoliate.	Arch Dimensions	\N
16a2272e-04ed-4c39-8857-46431bae67b9	orthodontics	BDS-I	Regarding the timing of the adolescent growth spurt, what is the average chronological difference between males and females?	{"Males peak 2 years earlier than females.","Females peak nearly 2 years earlier than males.","Both sexes peak at exactly age 12.","Males finish growth 5 years earlier than females."}	1	Despite individual variation, puberty and the adolescent growth spurt occur on average nearly 2 years earlier in girls than in boys.	Puberty Timing	\N
eba90f1c-df9e-410e-8c26-3e5823afaef5	orthodontics	BDS-I	In female patients, the onset of menstruation (menarche) clinically indicates that:	{"The growth spurt is just beginning.","The patient is exactly at peak height velocity.","Peak height velocity has already occurred and growth is decelerating.","Facial growth is 100% complete."}	2	Menarche always follows the peak velocity of the adolescent growth spurt, serving as an excellent indicator that the fastest phase of growth has passed.	Puberty Timing	\N
