635cf110-4e3d-404c-972a-88894c6ce35c	orthodontics	BDS-I	The clinical description "bimaxillary dentoalveolar protrusion" specifically means:	{"The maxilla is prognathic and the mandible is retrognathic.","Both upper and lower teeth protrude, causing prominent, everted lips.","The chin and nose are excessively prominent.","There is a severe anterior open bite."}	1	Bimaxillary protrusion means the teeth in both jaws protrude. Clinically, this is expressed as prominent and everted upper and lower lips.	Macro-Esthetics	\N
