993248f1-8e4b-4019-adb7-2fd545d2e8e3	public_health	BDS-I	During an oral health survey, an examiner notices that their diagnosis of dental fluorosis fluctuates between the morning and afternoon sessions. This is an issue of:	{"Inter-examiner reliability","Intra-examiner reliability",Sensitivity,Specificity}	1	Intra-examiner reliability refers to the consistency of a single examiner’s findings when evaluating the same subjects at different times.	General Epidemiology	\N
aeafe8ea-819b-49e2-be0c-4425b6ca45a2	public_health	BDS-I	A study observes that countries with high sugar consumption also have high DMFT scores, without individual-level data. This is an example of:	{"Cohort study","Case-control study","Ecological study","Clinical trial"}	2	Ecological studies use the population or country as the unit of analysis rather than the individual, often leading to the "ecological fallacy."	General Epidemiology	\N
