2c05b3b0-eb98-4e00-a3f7-ec11cd28e16f	public_health	BDS-I	"Quaternary Prevention" in the context of modern dentistry refers to:	{"Preventing caries","Preventing oral cancer","Protecting patients from over-medicalization","Rehabilitating tooth loss"}	2	Quaternary prevention aims to protect patients from unnecessary medical/dental interventions and ethical over-treatment.	General Epidemiology	\N
e7eacfe1-f5fb-4cc7-8f09-200c1ac4ead4	public_health	BDS-I	According to Dr. Rekha P. Shenoy, which index is "Reversible"?	{DMFT,"Dean’s Fluorosis Index","Gingival Index (Loe and Silness)","Community Caries Index"}	2	Gingival inflammation can return to health with treatment, whereas caries (DMFT) and fluorosis (Dean's) are permanent/irreversible records.	Indices in Dental Epidemiology	\N
1484725a-12bc-426a-8df3-8abfe451a652	public_health	BDS-I	In a population of 2,000, 1,200 people are tobacco users. 120 of these users have leukoplakia, while only 10 non-users have it. What is the Relative Risk (RR)?	{12,10,8,2}	0	RR = (Incidence in exposed / Incidence in unexposed). (120/1200) / (10/800) = 0.1 / 0.0125 = 8. (Correction: (120/1200)=0.1; (10/800)=0.0125. 0.1/0.0125 = 8).	General Epidemiology	\N
44c2b48a-1d08-44d0-bc71-c95c42b2edfd	public_health	BDS-I	The "Hopewood House Study" was significant because it demonstrated:	{"Caries can be reduced by water fluoridation","Caries can be reduced by a vegetarian diet and low refined carbs","Caries is infectious","Sealants work"}	1	This longitudinal study of children in Australia showed that even without fluoride, a strict diet low in sugar drastically reduced caries.	Epidemiology, Etiology and Prevention of Dental Caries	\N
56ce6942-6720-4918-95a6-1cc200880805	public_health	BDS-I	Which of the following is NOT a component of the "World Health Organization (WHO) definition" of Health?	{"Physical well-being","Mental well-being","Financial well-being","Social well-being"}	2	The WHO defines health as physical, mental, and social well-being, not merely the absence of disease.	General Epidemiology	\N
dac3e8e8-f9dd-40a6-b5b5-4e6f1b06603d	public_health	BDS-I	"Primary Prevention" for Malocclusion, as per Dr. Seema Iyyer Bhalajhi, includes:	{"Space maintainers","Fixed mechanotherapy","Le Fort osteotomy","Serial extraction"}	0	Space maintainers prevent the development of malocclusion following premature tooth loss, thus acting before the disease onset.	Epidemiology, Etiology and Prevention of Malocclusion	\N
a2c19e1d-d862-4896-a325-a748d6e3d836	public_health	BDS-I	When studying the epidemiology of Periodontal Disease, "Calculus" is best described as:	{"The primary agent","A non-etiological factor","A secondary etiologic factor (promoting plaque)","A systemic factor"}	2	Calculus does not cause disease by itself but provides a rough surface that facilitates plaque (the primary agent) accumulation.	Epidemiology, Etiology and Prevention of Periodontal Disease	\N
f0ab79d6-07ce-470c-b4ad-993e0a9368aa	public_health	BDS-I	The most common histological type of oral cancer worldwide is:	{Adenocarcinoma,"Squamous cell carcinoma","Verrucous carcinoma","Basal cell carcinoma"}	1	Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) accounts for over 90% of all oral malignancies.	Epidemiology, Etiology and Prevention of Oral Cancer	\N
