66dad47c-ced9-45a0-a7d6-284e902a8cee	public_health	BDS-I	The "Epidemiological Triad" for Malocclusion: "Premature loss of primary teeth" belongs to:	{Agent,Host,Environment,Vector}	2	While inherent genetics are Host, external factors like dental trauma or early extraction are part of the Environment.	Epidemiology, Etiology and Prevention of Malocclusion	\N
ea208fa8-acbd-41d1-a1f8-7bd6ddd61580	public_health	BDS-I	To determine the optimum fluoride level for a city with an average maximum temperature of 30°C, the "Galagan and Vermillion" formula is used. This formula is based on:	{Rainfall,"Water consumption relative to temperature","Age of the child",Diet}	1	The formula ppm = 0.34 / E (where E is estimated water intake based on temperature) accounts for the fact that people in hotter climates drink more water.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
dd988d87-b1db-428e-9191-bfc1eeb2b96e	public_health	BDS-I	A 15kg child accidentally ingests 200ml of a 0.05% NaF mouthrinse. Based on the Safely Tolerable Dose (STD) of 5mg F/kg, what is the clinical status?	{"The dose is safe","The dose exceeds the STD","The dose exceeds the CLD","Not enough information"}	1	0.05% NaF = 0.5 mg/ml. Total F = 200 * 0.5 = 100 mg. Child's weight = 15kg. STD = 15 * 5 = 75 mg. Since 100mg > 75mg, the child has exceeded the STD and needs immediate monitoring.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
61e3523e-c2c8-44de-a60d-9f256ea7b0e3	public_health	BDS-I	When applying 1.23% Acidulated Phosphate Fluoride (APF) gel, which of the following is crucial for the "etching" effect that enhances fluoride uptake?	{"1.23% NaF","0.1 M Orthophosphoric acid","pH of 7.0","Stannous ions"}	1	APF gel contains 0.1 M orthophosphoric acid, which lowers the pH to 3.5, slightly etching the enamel to facilitate fluoride entry.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
6630ec48-bddb-4136-9fd2-59eee2eee287	public_health	BDS-I	Which fluoride compound is known to cause a "metallic taste" and potential staining of tooth-colored restorations?	{"Sodium Fluoride (NaF)","Stannous Fluoride (SnF2)","Amine Fluoride","APF Gel"}	1	Stannous fluoride can cause extrinsic staining and has an unpleasant metallic taste due to the tin ion.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
05ab7e30-9bf2-462a-8609-5842dc4bf500	public_health	BDS-I	The "Halo Effect" (or Diffusion Effect) in fluoridation refers to:	{"The white halo around a fluorosed tooth","Benefits to a non-fluoridated community from food/drinks processed in a fluoridated area","Protection of the root surface","The glow of healthy enamel"}	1	People living in non-fluoridated areas receive fluoride through commercially processed beverages/foods from fluoridated areas.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
