899fd184-3513-4a6a-b024-cc758071ff71	public_health	BDS-I	In the "Nalgonda Technique" for defluoridation, the two primary chemicals added to water are:	{"Alum and Chlorine","Alum and Lime","Fluorine and Alum","Lime and Soda"}	1	Alum (coagulant) and Lime (disinfectant/buffer) are used to precipitate fluoride from water.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
9cd151a5-8361-4e54-a81c-9e049e308631	public_health	BDS-I	For a 5-year-old child living in an area with 0.4 ppm fluoride in the water, the daily supplemental fluoride dosage recommended is:	{"0.25 mg","0.50 mg","1.00 mg",None}	0	Standard charts (ADA/AAP) recommend 0.25 mg for children aged 3-6 years in areas with 0.3-0.6 ppm F.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
f63c127b-3234-409d-b6a8-717d8a97a47e	public_health	BDS-I	APF gel is contraindicated in patients with:	{"Heavy plaque","Porcelain or Composite restorations","Orthodontic brackets","History of asthma"}	1	The 0.1M orthophosphoric acid can etch and roughen the surface of porcelain and composite materials.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
76c32df5-0c9d-4a70-817b-41d58e9d4bbb	public_health	BDS-I	Fluoride varnish like "Duraphat" contains a fluoride concentration of:	{"1,000 ppm","12,300 ppm","22,600 ppm","5,000 ppm"}	2	Duraphat contains 5% Sodium Fluoride, which equates to 22.6 mg/ml or 22,600 ppm.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
73aa9ad0-1152-4ea3-b211-110af08765e5	public_health	BDS-I	What is the "Certainly Lethal Dose" (CLD) of fluoride for a 70kg adult?	{"1-2 grams","5-10 grams","32-64 mg","500 mg"}	1	The CLD is estimated at 32-64 mg of fluoride per kg of body weight, totaling 5-10 grams for an average adult.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
21a474f7-7fef-4ca9-b43d-ed46bb663f30	public_health	BDS-I	The primary mechanism of fluoride's "Post-eruptive" action is:	{"Making the tooth larger","Promoting remineralization of enamel","Changing the shape of fissures","Strengthening the pulp"}	1	Post-eruptively, fluoride works topically to inhibit demineralization and promote remineralization of early lesions.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
382b03ee-756f-4bf4-aeae-3a590f5189e7	public_health	BDS-I	Which fluoride compound is most commonly used in community "Milk Fluoridation" programs?	{"Stannous fluoride","Sodium fluoride",APF,"Silver Diamine Fluoride"}	1	NaF is the standard compound used for both water and milk fluoridation programs.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
17038ba8-d64a-4c7a-90ca-87dad05c81d7	public_health	BDS-I	"Dental Fluorosis" is a developmental disturbance of enamel. It can only occur during which period?	{"Post-eruptive maturation","Pre-eruptive mineralization","After the age of 12","During pregnancy only"}	1	Enamel fluorosis occurs due to excessive F ingestion during the calcification/mineralization phase of enamel formation.	Fluorides in Preventive Dentistry	\N
