b0577bae-83b9-45ab-83c2-ff3bd89c448d	public_health	BDS-I	In a "Triple Blind" clinical trial, who among the following is unaware of the treatment group assignments?	{"Subject and Investigator","Subject, Investigator, and Data Analyst","Investigator and Data Analyst","Subject only"}	1	Triple blinding adds an extra layer of protection by ensuring the person analyzing the data does not know which group is which, eliminating analytical bias.	General Epidemiology	\N
430ed2c8-be2e-482e-a1c5-d05df10a1469	public_health	BDS-I	The "Attributable Risk" is a measure used to determine:	{"The odds of having a disease","The number of cases that can be prevented if a risk factor is removed","The strength of association in a case-control study","The prevalence of a condition"}	1	Attributable risk indicates the extent to which the disease is due to the exposure; it is the difference in incidence between exposed and non-exposed groups.	General Epidemiology	\N
