ba10b4f3-29ab-4619-b8af-119510b31545	oral_surgery	BDS-I	In the management of Distraction Osteogenesis (DO), what is the most likely consequence of initiating a distraction rate of 2 mm per day instead of the standard 1 mm?	{"Rapid consolidation of regenerate bone","Development of a fibrous non-union","Excessive formation of immature bone","Improved mineralization of the callus"}	1	The standard distraction rate is 1 mm/day. A faster rate (e.g., 2 mm/day) often leads to a fibrous non-union because the regenerate tissue cannot keep up, while a slower rate (0.5 mm/day) may lead to premature consolidation.	Distraction Osteogenesis	\N
