4003e0ef-80e1-4705-9e87-1d9098188395	oral_surgery	BDS-I	Total maxillary osteotomy (Le Fort I) was historically staged to preserve blood supply. Modern research demonstrates that a single-stage procedure is safe as long as:	{"The descending palatine arteries are never ligated","A soft tissue pedicle is maintained in the palate and gingiva","Bone grafts are placed simultaneously to enhance revascularization","The maxilla is not advanced more than 5 mm"}	1	Reversal of normal blood flow occurs via transosseous and soft tissue collateral circulation (anastomosing plexuses of the gingiva, palate, and sinus) as long as the soft tissue pedicles are maintained.	Orthognathic Surgery	\N
