d5c1c9e9-66ef-4d07-9701-85b584cef06c	oral_surgery	BDS-I	Under the Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA), a practitioner on-call for a hospital has a primary legal duty to:	{"Provide free dental care to all indigent patients in the community","Only treat patients who are established in their private practice","Provide stabilizing treatment for emergency medical conditions","Report all HIPAA violations discovered during emergency consults"}	2	EMTALA imposes four duties on hospitals and on-call practitioners, the most critical being to provide a medical screening exam and stabilizing treatment for emergency conditions regardless of ability to pay.	Medicolegal	\N
ce86ce73-77de-4da5-8ace-29f0c7040ecc	oral_surgery	BDS-I	In modern rhytidectomy (face lift) procedures, the "workhorse" layer for achieving durable facial rejuvenation and avoiding a "pulled" skin appearance is the:	{Dermis,"SMAS (Superficial Musculoaponeurotic System)","Deep cervical fascia",Periosteum}	1	Modern facial rejuvenation focuses on manipulating the SMAS layer to provide structural support, which is more durable and looks more natural than merely tightening the skin.	Facial Cosmetic Surgery	\N
510db00d-0587-4f0a-92a5-8c8f5cecf1ba	oral_surgery	BDS-I	Recombinant human bone morphogenetic protein-2 (rhBMP-2) is frequently used in reconstruction. What is the standard carrier for this osteoinductive material?	{"Polymethyl methacrylate (PMMA)","Non-resorbable PTFE membrane","Absorbable collagen sponge (ACS)","Autogenous cortical bone chips"}	2	rhBMP-2 is typically placed on carriers, usually absorbable collagen sponges, which facilitate placement and allow the protein to adhere to the site after reconstitution.	Reconstructive Surgery	\N
4358b6a0-312a-45ea-b5e2-43ec6c0f0d54	oral_surgery	BDS-I	According to Limited English Proficiency (LEP) regulations, a dental practice MUST provide translated vital written documents if a language group constitutes:	{"1% of the practice","5% of the practice or 1,000 persons","10 persons regardless of practice size","Only if the patient requests them in writing"}	1	Translations for vital documents are required if an eligible LEP group constitutes 5% of the practice or 1,000 persons, whichever is less.	Practice Management	\N
086d9605-7413-40f7-b736-0b3b2463c563	oral_surgery	BDS-I	In the legal concept of "material risk," a risk must be disclosed to a patient during informed consent if:	{"It occurs in more than 50% of surgical cases","It is taught as a standard of care in all dental schools","A reasonable person would attach significance to it in decision-making","The dentist has personally experienced the complication before"}	2	A risk is "material" when a reasonable person is likely to attach significance to it in assessing whether to have the proposed therapy, regardless of whether it is "customary" in the profession to discuss it.	Medicolegal	\N
523ddb5e-d3c2-4078-82bb-d08d2e13aa00	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	According to the "Guyton Model," what is the true independent variable that regulates cardiac output?	{"Right atrial pressure","Heart rate","The oxygen needs of the body tissues","Mean arterial pressure"}	0	Guyton overturned conventional wisdom by proving that tissue oxygen need, not the heart itself, is the primary regulator of CO.	Cardiovascular	\N
a7ad677d-20be-4daa-8888-f29e43051ae2	oral_surgery	BDS-I	During a blepharoplasty procedure, which extremely rare complication is considered an absolute surgical emergency due to the risk of permanent blindness?	{"Dry eye syndrome (xerophthalmia)","Ectropion (eyelid turning outward)","Retrobulbar/orbital hematoma","Suture exfoliation"}	2	An orbital hematoma, though extremely rare, can cause pressure on the optic nerve and lead to blindness if not identified and treated (decompressed) immediately.	Facial Cosmetic Surgery	\N
e7a2d94e-38d7-4d6c-bb9c-99b54bf07fe9	oral_surgery	BDS-I	When placing two standard-diameter (4-mm) implants between two natural teeth, what is the MINIMUM mesial-distal space required to maintain biological health?	{"10 mm","12 mm","14 mm","16 mm"}	2	According to the source, 14 mm is the minimum space: 1.5 mm between each tooth and implant (total 3 mm), 4 mm for each implant (total 8 mm), and 3 mm between the two implants.	Implant Spacing	\N
9502f74d-a50e-4258-8104-1e2e6d4454a9	oral_surgery	BDS-I	In Distraction Osteogenesis, the "rhythm" of distraction refers to:	{"The total amount of bone generated per day","The duration of the latency period","The number of times the appliance is activated each day","The frequency of follow-up visits during consolidation"}	2	The "rate" is the total activation per day (e.g., 1 mm), while the "rhythm" is the timing of that activation (e.g., 0.5 mm twice daily).	Distraction Osteogenesis	\N
