b6cc60e2-732c-476e-9919-24c855a0a0b9	oral_surgery	BDS-I	According to the Two-Phase Theory of Osteogenesis, Phase II bone regeneration typically begins:	{"Within the first 24 hours","In the second week","After the first month","Only after functional loading"}	1	Phase I arises from surviving transplanted cells, while Phase II involves angiogenesis and fibroblastic proliferation from the graft bed starting in the second week.	Bone Grafting	\N
