9df8af06-20a0-422c-bd83-8f8f79400afe	anatomy	BDS-I	During tooth development, which of the following tissues is uniquely derived from the ectoderm, while the others are derived from neural crest cells?	{Dentin,"Dental Pulp",Enamel,Cementum}	2	Enamel is derived from the ectoderm (oral epithelium). All other hard and soft tissues of the tooth, including dentin, pulp, cementum, and the periodontal ligament, are derived from neural crest cells.	Oral Embryology	\N
e915853a-5381-4e19-be2d-3bd3e77c7d8f	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient presents with a deviation of the tongue to the right side upon protrusion. However, the ability to elevate the posterior part of the tongue is intact. Which muscle and nerve are likely spared?	{"Genioglossus - Hypoglossal nerve","Hyoglossus - Glossopharyngeal nerve","Palatoglossus - Vago-accessory complex","Styloglossus - Hypoglossal nerve"}	2	All muscles of the tongue are supplied by the Hypoglossal nerve (XII) except the palatoglossus. The palatoglossus is a muscle of the soft palate and is supplied by the pharyngeal plexus (vago-accessory complex).	Muscle & Nerve Supply	\N
