3055e4f5-560c-449a-b39c-2dc05684d1c4	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient has "Hyperacusis" (normal sounds appear too loud). This is due to paralysis of which muscle?	{"Tensor palati",Stapedius,"Tensor tympani",Salpingopharyngeus}	1	The stapedius muscle dampens vibrations; its paralysis (facial nerve) leads to hyperacusis.	Ear	\N
3c1cc7e5-af10-42f8-9c6f-ac2b91159058	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient has a "Port wine stain" on the angle of the jaw. Which nerve supplies this area?	{"Mandibular nerve (V3)","Maxillary nerve (V2)","Great Auricular nerve","Transverse Cervical nerve"}	2	The skin over the angle of the jaw is supplied by the great auricular nerve (C2, C3), not the trigeminal.	Clinical Anatomy	\N
1a2a62a2-414f-46f4-8df1-181f58ede25f	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient with "Tonsillitis" has referred pain in the ear. Which nerve carries the sensory impulses from the tonsil?	{Vagus,Glossopharyngeal,Trigeminal,Facial}	1	The glossopharyngeal nerve (IX) provides sensory supply to the palatine tonsil.	Pharynx	\N
61eaf0b1-b670-45da-bddb-434ecca91438	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient has a "deviated tongue" to the side of the lesion and the tongue looks shrunken. This is a sign of:	{"UMN lesion of XII","LMN lesion of XII","IX nerve lesion","X nerve lesion"}	1	An infranuclear (LMN) unilateral lesion of the hypoglossal nerve causes deviation and atrophy.	Tongue	\N
5d6bf641-582d-40af-a9fa-1c6a7ec173a6	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient presents with "Epistaxis" and nasal obstruction from a medial growth of a tumor. Which sinus is involved?	{Frontal,Ethmoidal,Maxillary,Sphenoidal}	2	Medial invasion of a maxillary sinus tumor encroaches the nasal cavity, causing epistaxis.	Paranasal Sinuses	\N
e3523848-047c-4357-8c19-ac25dacb9cce	anatomy	BDS-I	A clinician is performing the "Adson’s test" for a suspected cervical rib. The patient feels numbness in her forearm. Diagnosis?	{"Bell's Palsy","Scalene syndrome","Horner's Syndrome","Frey's Syndrome"}	1	Scalene syndrome is caused by compression of the brachial plexus and subclavian artery, often by a cervical rib.	Clinical Anatomy	\N
025f2fe9-2f13-4a8b-9e7e-57c421f6ed4f	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient has "Sialadenitis." What is this condition?	{"Inflammation of tonsils","Inflammation of salivary glands","Inflammation of the tongue","Inflammation of the larynx"}	1	Sialadenitis is the inflammation of the salivary glands.	Salivary Glands	\N
d14a8e05-bf44-49c6-bc63-8e3a5edfa65c	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient has a "Mucocele" on the oral mucosa. What is the common cause?	{"Bacterial infection","Severance of a minor salivary gland duct","Calculi in Stenson's duct","Viral infection"}	1	Mucoceles result from the severance of a minor salivary gland duct and pooling of saliva in tissues.	Salivary Glands	\N
