48c61c20-1e4c-40bd-b02e-5569e5b0df9d	anatomy	BDS-I	A child is a "mouth breather" and has a "toneless voice." The clinician suspects "Adenoids." Where are these located?	{Oropharynx,Nasopharynx,Laryngopharynx,"Oral cavity"}	1	Adenoids are located in the nasopharynx.	Pharynx	\N
34388e2b-e756-4cb8-97f7-cb8e7334241f	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient has "Retinal detachment." Histologically, what is separating?	{"The retina from the choroid","The outer pigmented layer from inner nine layers","The lens from the iris","The sclera from the choroid"}	1	Retinal detachment is an inter-retinal detachment where the inner nine layers separate from the outer pigmented layer.	Ophthalmology	\N
44fec731-520c-4ede-8ffb-eb12a6deec69	anatomy	BDS-I	A patient has "Glaucoma." What is the anatomical cause?	{"Lens opacity","High intraocular pressure","Retinal hemorrhage","Optic nerve inflammation"}	1	Glaucoma involves high intraocular pressure often related to aqueous humor drainage.	Ophthalmology	\N
