ad30aed0-ea2c-4c44-aba8-186a14336c6d	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	In Sickle Cell Anemia (HbS), what happens to the hemoglobin molecule under low oxygen tension (Deoxygenated state)?	{"It dissociates into alpha and beta monomers","It polymerizes into fibers that distort the RBC","It binds more tightly to 2,3-BPG, causing cell lysis","It undergoes spontaneous RNA editing"}	1	In deoxygenated HbS, the substitution of valine for glutamate causes molecules to polymerize into fibers, creating the sickle shape.	Hemoglobinopathy	\N
