560ce613-473c-4e20-93e7-146d8bef5d5e	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	In Scurvy, bleeding gums occur because Vitamin C is a necessary cofactor for:	{"Gamma-carboxylation of glutamic acid","Hydroxylation of Proline and Lysine","Glycosylation of collagen precursors","Cleavage of N-terminal signal sequences"}	1	Vitamin C is essential for lysyl and prolyl hydroxylases, which stabilize the triple helix of collagen.	Vitamins / Collagen	\N
c8a530c3-badf-47d9-94cf-6a30d043424b	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	In the visual cycle, what is the specific role of 11-cis-retinal?	{"It acts as a nuclear hormone receptor","It binds to Opsin to form Rhodopsin","It prevents oxidative damage to the lens","It is converted directly into Retinoic acid"}	1	11-cis-retinal combines with opsin to form rhodopsin; it isomerizes to all-trans-retinal when exposed to light.	Vitamins	\N
