b841af08-7be9-4071-b3bf-4f216f746b0c	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	Why is Ethanol used to treat Methanol poisoning?	{"It neutralizes formaldehyde","It acts as a competitive inhibitor of Alcohol Dehydrogenase","It increases the renal excretion of methanol","It stabilizes the retinal membranes"}	1	Ethanol has a higher affinity for Alcohol Dehydrogenase, acting as a competitive inhibitor to prevent methanol conversion to toxic formaldehyde.	Clinical Toxicology	\N
