6d5cb1bb-c761-4000-8e97-bc41ff228a6f	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	Why does Vitamin B6 deficiency lead to the excretion of Xanthurenic acid in urine?	{"B6 directly converts xanthurenate to kynurenine","PLP is a cofactor for kynureninase in the tryptophan pathway","B6 inhibits the alternative xanthurenate pathway","Xanthurenate is a metabolic byproduct of isoniazid"}	1	In B6 deficiency, the kynureninase enzyme fails; tryptophan metabolism is diverted to an alternative pathway, producing xanthurenic acid.	Vitamins / Amino Acids	\N
220b9492-7f24-40c5-b683-457d16dc0cc1	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	A child with "Brittle Bone Disease" and blue sclera has a mutation in the synthesis of which collagen type?	{"Type I","Type II","Type III","Type IV"}	0	Osteogenesis Imperfecta (Brittle Bone Disease) is primarily caused by defects in Type I Collagen, which is found in bones and sclera.	Collagenopathy	\N
958dd4e4-81f3-40f4-a42d-e3122aa69f8e	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	A patient with suspected Wilson’s Disease will show which plasma result?	{"Elevated Serum Copper","Decreased Serum Ceruloplasmin","Normal Urinary Copper","Elevated Serum ALP"}	1	Wilson’s Disease is characterized by decreased serum ceruloplasmin and increased urinary copper excretion.	Mineral Metabolism	\N
