959eeca9-aa8f-4881-93ae-1181e0fb4a42	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	A patient with hyperuricemia is treated with Allopurinol. What is the mechanism of action?	{"It increases the renal excretion of urate","It is a suicide inhibitor of Xanthine Oxidase","It prevents the absorption of dietary purines","It converts uric acid into allantoin"}	1	Allopurinol is a structural analog of hypoxanthine; it is converted to alloxanthine, which acts as a suicide inhibitor of Xanthine Oxidase.	Nucleotide Metabolism	\N
