488e8152-d671-436f-a2cb-ff390cfc86e4	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	In DKA, why does the patient's breath have a "fruity" odor?	{"Exhalation of acetoacetate","Exhalation of acetone","Breakdown of lactic acid in the lungs","High blood glucose concentration"}	1	Acetone, a volatile ketone body produced by the spontaneous decarboxylation of acetoacetate, is exhaled in the breath.	Carbohydrate Metabolism	\N
