51644697-a1c7-4004-b375-ef673d9d2587	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	Which vacutainer is recommended for glucose estimation to prevent "spontaneous glycolysis"?	{"Red cap","Lavender cap","Gray cap","Light blue cap"}	2	The Gray cap vacutainer contains sodium fluoride, which acts as an antiglycolytic agent.	Clinical Lab	\N
5b4a03bf-da7a-41eb-8ec8-2b835f82788d	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	In "RNA Editing," the liver produces ApoB-100, while the intestine produces ApoB-48. This is due to:	{"Alternative splicing of the gene","Cytidine deaminase converting a CAA codon to UAA","Post-translational cleavage by proteases","Deletion of exons in intestinal cells"}	1	RNA editing in the intestine converts a CAA (Glutamine) codon to a UAA (Stop) codon, resulting in the shorter ApoB-48 protein.	Molecular Biology	\N
