2b229650-b14d-4975-8f20-66da952d69c0	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	"Malignant PKU" is distinct from classic PKU because it does not respond to diet and involves a deficiency of:	{"Phenylalanine hydroxylase","Tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4)","Tyrosine transaminase","Homogentisate oxidase"}	1	Malignant PKU is due to a deficiency of the cofactor BH4, which is needed not only for phenylalanine metabolism but also for neurotransmitter synthesis.	Amino Acid Metabolism	\N
db396f0f-2205-4956-ac4c-efc18a23b99d	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	A patient with high-fat intake shows a "creamy layer" floating on top of their plasma after overnight storage at 4°C. This layer consists of:	{LDL,VLDL,Chylomicrons,HDL}	2	Chylomicrons have the lowest density and are largest; they float to the top of refrigerated plasma, forming a characteristic "creamy layer."	Lipid Metabolism	\N
