a2425619-3558-47ef-9703-09a5bbdb0f90	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	A "Second Wind Phenomenon" after a few minutes of exercise is characteristic of which disease?	{"Von Gierke's",Pompe's,McArdle's,Her's}	2	In McArdle's disease (Muscle phosphorylase deficiency), patients experience cramps initially. After a few minutes, they improve as the body mobilizes blood-borne glucose and fatty acids ("second wind").	Carbohydrate Metabolism	\N
d872d43c-1532-4204-a147-62c0a7a3d406	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	Which laboratory finding is expected in a patient with severe Vitamin D deficiency (Rickets)?	{"High Serum Phosphate","Low Alkaline Phosphatase","High Serum Calcium","Low Serum 25-hydroxycholecalciferol"}	3	Rickets is characterized by low 25(OH)D levels, low phosphate, and elevated alkaline phosphatase (a vain attempt by osteoblasts at bone formation).	Vitamins / Minerals	\N
0fc9d6c2-f539-4368-9b30-b1300544928f	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	Why is Ethanol used as a "twisted" treatment for Methanol poisoning?	{"It neutralizes the acid produced","It acts as a competitive inhibitor of Alcohol Dehydrogenase","It increases renal clearance of formaldehyde","It prevents the oxidation of NADH"}	1	Ethanol has a higher affinity for Alcohol Dehydrogenase than methanol. It outcompetes methanol, preventing the formation of toxic formaldehyde.	Clinical Toxicology	\N
