794496c9-8de9-4427-b7dd-e7716fd8ca38	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	Which protein is the earliest marker for Myocardial Infarction, appearing within 4–6 hours?	{CK-MB,"Troponin I",LDH1,Myoglobin}	3	Myoglobin is the earliest marker to appear in the blood after MI, though it lacks cardiac specificity.	Clinical Enzymology	\N
056ab51a-126d-4a89-ade1-48a0ebaf474c	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	A patient with Hartnup’s disease might develop "Blue Diaper Syndrome" because:	{"Tryptophan is excreted in urine","Indican in the urine oxidizes to indigo blue","B6 deficiency causes blue pigment","Niacin supplements turn urine blue"}	1	Unabsorbed tryptophan is converted by bacteria to indoles, which are absorbed and excreted as Indican. Exposure to air oxidizes Indican to indigo blue, causing the "blue diaper."	Amino Acid Metabolism	\N
