a4d480bc-7ba3-4c05-89c3-97bb95f944b2	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	A primary tooth fails to exfoliate because its root has fused directly to the alveolar bone. What is the clinical term for this condition?	{Impaction,Ankylosis,Diastema,Dilaceration}	1	Ankylosis occurs when the tooth root fuses with the underlying hard tissue (bony socket), preventing eruption or shedding.	Eruption and Shedding	\N
