4790c531-cc96-4944-ba73-4513da618ffd	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	During enamel production, what is the specific chronological order of calcification within the tooth crown?	{"Cervical to Incisal","Incisal/Cusp tips to Cervical","Random distribution","Simultaneously across the crown"}	1	The cusp tips are the first areas of enamel to calcify, and the cervical enamel is the last.	Amelogenesis	\N
