fc028940-74ff-46b2-a206-f6b66e38b8b5	physiology_biochem	BDS-I	Damage to glomerular capillaries in chronic diabetes logically leads to edema because:	{"It increases blood colloid pressure","It decreases Bowman’s capsule pressure","Proteins lost in urine decrease blood colloid osmotic pressure","It increases renal blood flow"}	0	Protein loss (proteinuria) causes a deficiency in blood colloid pressure, which prevents fluid from returning to capillaries, resulting in interstitial fluid accumulation (edema).	Renal Physiology	\N
