156e48e4-180e-4f47-a169-1924eb034393	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	The "smear layer" is a clinical consideration during cavity preparation. What is its primary effect on dentin permeability?	{"Increases it","Decreases it","No effect","Eliminates tubules"}	1	The smear layer acts as a natural plug, significantly decreasing the permeability of dentin by covering the tubule openings.	Dentin Permeability	\N
