2a876f47-5a14-46a1-b095-6d3bcce86071	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	Which structural feature of enamel is formed by the rhythmic deposition of enamel matrix and is considered a "growth line"?	{"Enamel tufts","Enamel lamellae","Striae of Retzius","Enamel spindles"}	2	The striae of Retzius are incremental growth lines in enamel, representing periodic intervals of matrix deposition.	Enamel Histology	\N
