c96a2aee-9682-4e10-afaa-ba25400b4fdf	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	Failure of the "nasal fin" to be penetrated by connective tissue growth results in which clinical defect?	{"Cleft palate","Bifid tongue","Cleft lip",Macroglossia}	2	The nasal fin is a zone of fusion between the medial nasal and maxillary processes. If connective tissue does not penetrate it, the lip could pull apart, causing a cleft.	Facial Clefts	\N
