fb8a6076-101a-4f44-a862-eb416c4649e0	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	The Primary Palate forms the roof of the:	{"Posterior oral cavity","Anterior oral cavity",Nasopharynx,"Maxillary sinus"}	1	Roof of the anterior portion of the primitive oral cavity.	Palate Development	\N
27ea8e77-5078-433d-ae75-445242c41c56	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	At which prenatal week do palatine shelves elevate and fuse?	{"5th week","7th week","9th week","12th week"}	2	Shelf elevation and fusion occur around the 9th week .	Palate Development	\N
2c8a24f4-6380-4e19-8d92-c959ebadb6e6	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	Which tooth is derived from the primary palate?	{"Maxillary Canine","Maxillary First Molar","Maxillary Central Incisor","Maxillary Second Premolar"}	2	The upper incisor teeth come from the primary palate .	Palate Development	\N
de9b6bea-c2b2-420b-bc57-55b7c7f24d44	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	Lingual papillae begin to appear at:	{"4th week","7th week","12th week","16th week"}	1	They appear early at about the 7th week .	Oral Mucosa	\N
5baebabd-3ac0-43db-af4c-e3f51b82a799	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	Which papillae are the last to be recognized?	{Circumvallate,Foliate,Filiform,Fungiform}	2	Filiform papillae are recognized later (10–12 weeks) .	Oral Mucosa	\N
e75201f1-06fb-41ab-ba14-51de2a626b55	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	The dental follicle gives rise to:	{Dentin,Enamel,"Cementum, PDL, and Alveolar bone","Dental lamina"}	2	Derivatives include cementum, PDL, and alveolar bone.	Tooth Development	\N
98a662a0-9047-49a7-87fa-9a224ae0ec04	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	The dental papilla is the primordium of:	{Enamel,"Dentin and Pulp",Cementum,"Alveolar bone"}	1	Formative organ of dentin and pulp.	Tooth Development	\N
6ac63bf5-16ac-4fca-bae2-2da67f0cb6c9	dental_anatomy	BDS-I	Inner Enamel Epithelium (IEE) cells differentiate into:	{Odontoblasts,Ameloblasts,Fibroblasts,Osteoblasts}	1	IEE cells become ameloblasts.	Histophysiology	\N
