3bfb2d1a-b2f7-494f-a832-1a59d5d11944	conservative_endo	BDS-IV	What is this feature, and what is its endodontic significance?	{"Palatogingival groove; can lead to localized periodontal-endodontic lesions","Mesial developmental groove; causes root fractures","Talon cusp; causes pulp necrosis","Cusp of Carabelli; no endodontic significance."}	0	The palatogingival groove is a developmental anomaly often found in maxillary lateral incisors that acts as a pathway for plaque, frequently leading to localized deep periodontal pockets and secondary endodontic involvement.		/api/uploads/d46187a66eb2a48b408ce76990d7e748.png
