a93f4201-a8fd-40af-a9aa-76b801e8f482	oral_med_rad	BDS-IV	On a bitewing radiograph, the proximal surfaces of the teeth appear overlapped\nWhat is the most likely cause?	{"Excessive vertical angulation","Incorrect horizontal angulation","Patient movement","Film bending."}	1	Horizontal angulation determines whether the central ray is directed through the contact points. If the ray is not parallel to the interproximal spaces, the proximal surfaces will overlap, as explained in standard radiographic technique protocols.		/api/uploads/538266ac64b2ef788ee559b0ef4a23ae.png
